s://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"V4 separates scenario-relative coverage, evidence verification and downstream composition. A fixed, separately declared scenario contract identifies requirements independently of the verifier/catalog inventory. The experiment demonstrates passing declared checks despite omitted requirements, with exact scope and authority boundaries.\n\nValidation: 54 scenarios (4 positive, 50 negative/unsupported), 24 tests in normal/repeat/Python -O, deterministic semantic outputs and 44 killed physical mutants per mode, zero survived/crashed in the corrected final experiment. Thirteen catalog deletions are detected as coverage alarms; 31 enforcement/guard removals allow their targeted unsupported claim. The initial development run's 13 generator crashes remain preserved separately and never count as kills.\n\nSame-evidence false authorizations: component-only 41/50; declared obligations 21/50; scenario-contract coverage plus composition 0/50. Missing-obligation controls detected 13/13. Ten real laboratory signatures are independently checked with Node/noble and Python/eth-account; the retained native zkIE proof is actually verified. Laboratory artifacts are not external observations.\n\nWYRIWE Section 5's conditional availability semantics are preserved; stronger provenance requirements are explicitly research policy. Current ERC-8274 and agent-ercs interface versions differ, so no conformant adapter/deployment is claimed. Coverage is relative to trusted contract adequacy, not universal completeness. Exploratory observation categories are not attributed to Echo or ordered into a hierarchy. Prior-art comparison does not establish scientific novelty.\n\nExternal chain remains PARTIAL_CHAIN_VERIFIED. No upstream vulnerability, general security benefit, full-chain success or external execution is claimed.\n\nBased on unmerged Draft PR #3 at 98ffba16730030c797c47766e13a5314181ba2f6 (which depends on PR #2). Main diff includes those dependencies; review v4-only changes from that SHA. Historical evidence is unchanged. Keep draft; do not merge automatically.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T18:07:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:14Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merged_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merge_commit_sha":"ee1143f2b8f669a88f36c736d20bb86c2ade950a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"trustless-ai:research/verification-obligation-coverage-v4","ref":"research/verification-obligation-coverage-v4","repo":{"id":1422280233,"node_id":"R_kgDOVMZGKQ","name":"verifiable-execution-claim-authorization","full_name":"trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization","owner":{"login":"trustless-ai","id":295405515,"node_id":"O_kgDOEZuHyw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295405515?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":